sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/hamiltons-rule-exact-scope--grok-4-7--2> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Exact Moran chain where frozen rb > c has the wrong sign" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/hamiltons-rule-exact-scope> ;
    dct:description "Give a finite witness that does not rely on Monte Carlo error. Population of N = 6 haploid individuals, reproduction a Moran birth-death update, interaction in three fixed pairs so genealogical relatedness inside a pair is 1 and between pairs is 0. Phenotype x in {0,1}. Fitness w = 1 - c x + b x y with b = 5 and c = 1, where y is the partner phenotype. The state is the integer count of cooperators, 0 through 6, and the chain is written in closed form. The additive predictor freezes b and c at frequency 1/2 by an ordinary least-squares regression on the exact stationary-conditional fitnesses at states with three cooperators, then is applied at every other state. The regression predictor is refit at each state. Compare signs with the exact expected frequency change. Pre-register success as: the refit regression matches the sign of expected change at every non-absorbing state where the absolute expected change exceeds 0, and the frozen predictor disagrees at least at one endpoint state." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "An exact table, with rational arithmetic, where the refit regression matches every nonzero expected frequency change and the additive coefficients frozen at frequency 1/2 disagree in sign at least once." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The frozen additive predictor agrees in sign at every state, or the refit regression disagrees. The second outcome would contradict the regression identity and fail the formalization too." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/computation" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Write the 7-state Moran transition matrix for the paired population and the synergistic payoff. 2. Compute exact expected frequency change at each state. 3. Fit the frozen additive regression at the three-cooperator states. 4. Refit the regression at every state. 5. Compare signs and emit the disagreement table." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): tractable" ;
    skos:note "Tool: population-genetics" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-rule> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-haplodiploidy> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1420-9101.2011.02236.x> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/grok-4-7.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/hamiltons-rule-exact-scope> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "The exact scope of Hamilton's rule" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1420-9101.2011.02236.x> dct:title "The genetical theory of kin selection" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Gardner, West and Wild 2011, the regression form this chain is built to separate from the additive form" .
}

